{"timestamp": "2025-09-06T03:34:53.002200", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Step 1: Convert item name to its index using the cookbook\n  try:\n    item_index = env.world.cookbook.index[item]\n  except KeyError:\n    print(f\"Error: Item '{item}' not found in the cookbook.\")\n    return []\n\n  # Step 2: Check if the item has a recipe; otherwise, it's likely a primitive and cannot be crafted\n  if item_index not in env.world.cookbook.recipes:\n    print(f\"Error: No recipe for item '{item}'. It may be a primitive.\")\n    return []\n  \n  # Step 3: Get all required primitives and their counts to craft the item\n  required_primitives = env.world.cookbook.primitives_for(item_index)\n  current_inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # Step 4: Collect all required primitives if they are not already in inventory\n  for primitive_index, count in required_primitives.items():\n    # Check if the current inventory has enough of this primitive\n    if current_inventory[primitive_index] < count:\n      # Determine the name of the primitive to collect\n      primitive_name = env.world.cookbook.index.get(primitive_index)\n      if not primitive_name:\n        print(f\"Error: Could not find name for primitive index {primitive_index}.\")\n        return []\n\n      # Collect the required amount of this primitive\n      actions.extend(collect(env, primitive_name))\n\n  # Step 5: Move to the workshop specified in the recipe and craft the item (USE action)\n  # Assuming the first available workshop can be used for crafting any item\n  workshop_index = env.world.workshop_indices[0]\n\n  if not next_to(env._current_state, workshop_index):\n    actions.extend(move(env, \"WORKSHOP\", workshop_index))\n\n  # Step 6: Use the USE action to craft the item\n  actions.append(env.world.cookbook.index[\"USE\"])\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
